{
  "symbol": "TDPOWERSYS",
  "name": "TD Power Systems Limited",
  "sector": "Industrials",
  "industry": "Capital Goods \u2014 Electrical Equipment",
  "isin": "",
  "thesis": {
    "bull_case": "TD Power Systems occupies a high-barrier niche in large custom AC/DC generators for captive power, gas turbines, hydro, and industrial motors \u2014 segments with scarce domestic competition \u2014 and stands to benefit directly from India's accelerating power-sector capex cycle (thermal, hydro, industrial). The debt-free balance sheet, a face-value stock split in Aug 2026, and four consecutive dividend payments (interim + final) signal confident management and strong internal cash generation. Export diversification to Europe and Asia provides a natural hedge against domestic capex cycles.",
    "bear_case": "Revenue is inherently lumpy because contracts are large, project-based, and have long manufacturing cycles, making short-term earnings volatile and difficult to predict. Global majors \u2014 ABB (Brush), Siemens Energy, Marelli \u2014 with larger R&D budgets and global manufacturing networks can undercut on price or win marquee projects, limiting pricing power. A slowdown in thermal or industrial capex (policy reversal, project cancellations) would sharply compress the order book with no quick offset.",
    "moat": "Narrow but durable moat built on proprietary engineering design capability for large custom electrical machines, high switching costs for OEM customers who qualify and validate suppliers over multi-year programmes, and limited domestic competition in the >1 MVA custom generator segment.",
    "key_risks": [
      "Project-based revenue lumpiness creates quarter-to-quarter earnings volatility and complicates valuation",
      "Raw-material inflation (copper, CRGO steel) on fixed-price contracts can materially compress margins if unhedged",
      "Customer and sector concentration: a pause in thermal or industrial capex \u2014 driven by policy shifts, grid over-capacity, or financing stress \u2014 directly dents order inflows"
    ],
    "investment_horizon": "12M",
    "last_reviewed": "2026-11-06"
  },
